-- title:
--   Maximal ideals preserved at crossings under base change
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ (i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$), and a package $\mathfrak{P} :$ `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, the residue field of $A$ being of characteristic $q$ and algebraically closed. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, equipped with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ onto the valuation subring of the inertia fixed field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{I_A}$ obtained by pulling back $A$, where $I_A$ is the image in $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$; let $\rho_O : R_q \to O$ be a ring map compatible, via $e_O$ and the inclusion $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{I_A} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the structure map $R_q \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$ be the map sending $o$ to the residue class of $e_O(o)$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two sections $\mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{comp}\,\kappa(A)\,(\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O)\,i$, $i = 0,1$, over the special fibre, and assume `hrat`: the composite of $O \to \Gamma$ of the $O$-side pullback projection, the germ at the image point of $n$ under `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`, and the residue map, is surjective onto the residue field of that stalk. Then for $i = 0,1$, the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal under the stalk map of `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ` at the image of $n$ under the $i$-th projection followed by the $i$-th section is the full maximal ideal of the stalk on the special fibre.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness of the base change $\mathfrak{X}_{\kappa} \to \mathfrak{X}_O$ at the two branches through a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model at level $N_0 q$: the maximal ideal of the stalk upstairs generates the maximal ideal of the stalk on the fibre, which is what makes the local rings at the branch points behave as expected after passing to the residue field of the inertia field. It feeds the analysis of node coordinates and crossing charts used to identify the special fibre of the model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_map_maximalIdeal_stalkMap_bcMap_eq_of_inertia_grain.lean

